*Constants* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

*Runtime Constants*

These constants are available at runtime with a clean chippy session:

''null'' - The number 0.
''false'' - The number 0, standard falsy value.
''true'' - The number 1, standard truthy value.

''err'' - Error marker string "__~err~__". Used and recommended to indicate operation failure.
''ok'' - Success marker string "__~ok~__". Used and recommended to indicate operation success.

*Core Constants*

''CHIPVR'' - Chippy version
''CHIPCN'' - Release codename for CHIPVR
''CHIPOS'' - Host operating system
''CHIPAR'' - Host architecture

*Bundle Constants*

''BUNDLERUN'' - Set to ''true'' when running from a bundle, ''false'' otherwise
''BUNDLEDIR'' - String path to extraction directory, ''err'' if not running in a bundle
''BUNDLEID'' - Bundle ID, ''null'' if not running in a bundle

See ''chippy doc bundles''
